  },
  "body": {
    "focus": "Registering the insrc server in a Vibe config that holds a top-level inline mcp_servers list produces a valid TOML file, from both the VS Code plugin (vscode-plugin/src/hosts/toml-mcp-writer.ts) and the daemon (upsertVibeProjectServer in src/daemon/mcp-register.ts). Every server already in the inline list and every other setting is kept, and insrc is registered once. Registering again changes nothing. Where a writer cannot safely bring a config into a valid form, it leaves the file untouched and reports the failure instead of writing an invalid file.",
    "producesLld": false,
    "commit": "739e70e98",
    "tasks": [
      {
        "id": "s1",
        "passed": false
      }
    ],
    "summary": "Both Vibe config writers now move an inline mcp_servers list into [[mcp_servers]] tables before adding the insrc server, through one shared helper, and leave a config they cannot fix untouched. Quoted and escaped key spellings are recognised. A full sweep did not complete, so failing and unreached test files were compared one by one against an untouched HEAD; 182 of 1,419 files fail or time out on both.",
